{{Quote|Troop reinforcements. Here we go.|Laren Joma, during the Battle of Scarif|audio=Reinforcements-Joma-RO.flac|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
'''Laren Joma''' was a [[human]] [[UT-60D U-wing starfighter/support craft|U-wing]] [[Rebel pilot|pilot]] for the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]]. Flying as [[Blue Eleven]] in [[Blue Squadron (Rebel Alliance)|Blue Squadron]], she often transported [[Rebel trooper|troops]] with the [[Iakaru]] [[Bistan]] as her door [[gunner]], nicknaming him "space monkey" and tolerating his exuberance due to his unerring aim. In [[1 BBY]], she was scrambled along with the rest of her [[squadron]] to aid [[Rogue One|rebels]] trying to [[Battle of Scarif|steal]] the [[Death Star plans|plans]] for the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] [[superweapon]] on the [[planet]] [[Scarif]].

Once in the [[Scarif system]], Joma and her co-[[pilot]], [[Taslet Colb]], flew their U-wing through the world's [[Shield Gate]] and then worked with the rest of Blue Squadron to neutralize a group of [[All Terrain Armored Cargo Transport]]s [[Ground warfare|attacking]] the rebels on the ground. Joma and Colb then delivered the ground reinforcements that the U-wing was carrying before [[Death|perishing]] when the [[starship]] was shot down by [[TIE/sk x1 experimental air superiority fighter|TIE strikers]].

==Biography==
===Scramble for Scarif===
{{Quote|Blue Squadron, get to the surface before they close that gate.|Raddus|audio=Raddus-BlueSquadron.flac|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
[[File:BlueSquadronPreGate-RO.png|thumb|left|300px|Laren Joma flew a U-wing in Blue Squadron at the Battle of Scarif.]]
Laren Joma was a [[human]] [[Warrant Officer]] in the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] who flew a [[Bistan's U-wing|UT-60D U-wing starfighter/support craft]] as [[Blue Eleven]] as part of the Alliance's mixed-[[Starship|vessel]] [[Blue Squadron (Rebel Alliance)|Blue Squadron]],<ref name="UVG" /> often transporting [[Rebel trooper|troops]] with the [[Iakaru]] [[Bistan]] as<ref name="Pilots">{{EncyclopediaCite|Pilots of the Rebel Alliance}}</ref> her<ref name="UVG" /> door [[gunner]].<ref name="Pilots" /> The [[squadron]] was stationed as part of the [[Massassi Group]] in the rebel's [[Great Temple]] base on the [[moon]] [[Yavin 4]]<ref name="UVG" /> and in [[1 BBY]]<ref name="Date" /> was partially mobilized for a [[Mission to Eadu|mission]] to attack an [[Eadu Energy Conversion Laboratory|Imperial facility]] on the [[planet]] [[Eadu]].<ref name="Rogue One" />

Shortly after the survivors from the mission returned, the [[Alliance Cabinet|Rebel Council]] that led the Alliance rejected calls to [[Battle of Scarif|attack]] another [[Citadel Tower|Imperial facility]] on the planet [[Scarif]] in order to try and [[Thief|steal]] the [[Death Star plans|plans]] for the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] [[superweapon]]. Despite this decision, a [[Rogue One|group]] of rebels went rogue and traveled to Scarif to steal the plans anyway. When Imperial transmissions concerning this attack reached Yavin 4, the [[Rebel Alliance Navy|Alliance fleet]] was scrambled under the command of [[Admiral]] [[Raddus]] to support the rebels on Scarif.<ref name="Rogue One" /> Blue Squadron was fully mobilized for the first [[time]] for the mission, with Joma [[Rebel pilot|piloting]] a U-Wing with [[Lieutenant]] [[Taslet Colb]] as her co-[[pilot]] and Bistan on the door [["Roba" M-45 repeating ion blaster|turret]]. Tasked with transporting rebel ground reinforcements, including [[Private]] [[Talwer]], [[Corporal]] [[Walea Timker]], and Corporal [[Rodma Maddel]], to deploy on Scarif,<ref name="UVG" /> Joma piloted the craft through [[hyperspace]] alongside the rest of the [[fleet]] to reach the [[Scarif system]].<ref name="Rogue One" />

===Walker wipeout===
{{Quote|U-wings, reinforce those troops on the beach. All fighters, on me. We have to shield them from air attack.|Antoc Merrick|audio=Uwings-Merrick-RO.flac|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
[[File:BlueSquadronBeaches-RO.png|thumb|right|300px|Joma and Blue Squadron destroyed Imperial walkers on Scarif.]]
Once they were in the [[Star system|system]], Raddus ordered Blue Squadron to head for Scarif's surface, which required them to pass through the Empire's [[planetary shield]] using a [[Shield Gate]]. Following [[Blue Leader]] [[Antoc Merrick]], Joma and the rest of the squadron then raced for the gate as the Empire began to close it. Both Merrick and Joma made it through the gate before it closed,<ref name="Rogue One" /> although hers was the only U-wing to do so;<ref name="HC71">{{HelmetCollectionCite|71|Weapons & Uniforms}}</ref> other members of the squadron crashed into the barrier or were forced to split off and join the [[Starfighter combat|fighting]] outside the shield.<ref name="Rogue One" />

Inside, those who had made it through formed up on Merrick and located the [[Alliance Military|rebel forces]] on the surface, who were under [[Ground warfare|attack]] from a group of [[All Terrain Armored Cargo Transport]]s. After Merrick destroyed one of the [[AT-series|walkers]] in a pass, the squadron circled back around and Joma split off to circle another [[walker]] and bring the U-Wing into a position where Bistan could open fire on one of the walker's [[Limb|leg]] joints. The Iakaru succeeded in destroying the joint, bringing down the whole vehicle as Joma joined back up with the squadron.<ref name="Rogue One" />

===Last landing===
{{Quote|We're going down!|Laren Joma|audio=GoingDown-Joma-RO.flac|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
[[File:UWingExplosion-RO.png|thumb|left|300px|Joma perished on Scarif when her U-wing was shot down.]]
With the walker threat neutralized, Merrick ordered Joma to drop off her reinforcements while he and the other [[starfighter]] pilots provided air cover. Joma hovered her craft low over one of Scarif's [[beach]]es in front of the rebel forces already fighting there. With a cheer, the [[trooper]]s on board exited the craft and joined their comrades before Joma took off again and re-joined the rest of Blue Squadron.<ref name="Rogue One" />

As the battle raged on, the squadron became more separated, with [[TIE/sk x1 experimental air superiority fighter|TIE strikers]] shooting down Merrick and other fighters. Four strikers then rushed head on at Joma's craft, with one shooting out the ventral port [[4J.7 fusial thrust engine|engine]]. As the U-wing hurtled toward the ground, Joma turned and shouted a warning to Bistan and the rest of her crew,<ref name="Rogue One" /> but the gunner, the pilot, and Colb were all [[Death|killed]]<ref name="Geektionary">''[[Star Wars: Geektionary: The Galaxy from A - Z]]''</ref> when the vessel exploded upon impact. Despite their heavy loses, the rebels managed to successfully recover the [[Death Star]] plans from Scarif and escape with them.<ref name="Rogue One" />

==Personality and traits==
Laren Joma had a stern nature that was reflected in her physical appearance.<ref name="Geektionary" /> However, she was also an even-keeled individual<ref name="UVG" /> who was happy in the company of others as long as they were professional, even if they differed greatly from her.<ref name="Geektionary" />

[[File:JomaCockpit-RO.png|thumb|right|300px|Laren Joma was a stern-looking pilot but showed remarkable composure.]]
For this reason, she tolerated the youthful exuberance of Bistan<ref name="Geektionary" />&mdash;who she jokingly<ref name="Topps">{{Topps|set=2018 Topps Star Wars Galactic Files|cardname=Laren Joma|link=https://www.tcdb.com/ViewCard.cfm/sid/170092/cid/11644237/2018-Topps-Star-Wars:-Galactic-Files-RO-44-Laren-Joma}}</ref> nicknamed "space monkey"&mdash;due to the Iakaru's unerring aim. While acting as his "delivery driver," she flew with a steady hand in order to aid the Iakaru's aim and keep those on board her vessel alive.<ref name="UVG" /> Cool-headed and generally unflappable,<ref name="Topps" /> she showed remarkable composure under the most difficult of circumstances.<ref name="Geektionary" /> Joma had light skin, [[Color|brown]] [[hair]], and brown [[eye]]s.<ref name="UVG" />

==Skills and abilities==
Joma had above-average intelligence with average speed and fighting abilities. Her strength and [[diplomat]]ic skills were slightly below average, and she was not [[Force-sensitive]].<ref name="Topps" />

==Equipment==
While piloting a U-wing,<ref name="Rogue One" /> Joma wore a blue [[flight suit]] with a white [[flak vest]], a white [[flight harness]], white [[glove]]s, and black [[boot]]s.<ref name="Pilots" /> Her [[flight helmet]] had red sides and a black central strip that was decorated with a red [[starbird]] at its front.<ref name="Rogue One" /> She also used a [[high-atmosphere specialist life support pack]] instead of the standard [[Novaldex]] [[Diagnostech life support unit]], as U-wings were often required to open their side doors at high altitudes in order to deploy [[troop]]s or allow their door gunner to fire.<ref name="HC71" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:UWingCockpit.png|thumb|right|300px|Laren Joma (right) was illustrated on the wrong side of the cockpit in ''Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide''.]]
Laren Joma first appeared in the [[Star Wars Anthology Series|Anthology Series]] film ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]'',<ref name="Rogue One" /> which was released on [[December 16]], [[2016]].<ref name="SW.com">{{SW|url=news/rebel-reading-rogue-one-books|text=Rebel Reading: A Guide to ''Rogue One'' Books|author=[[James Floyd|Floyd, James]]|date=2016-12-14}}</ref> Prior to the release of the film, footage of Joma's U-wing in action was first revealed in the Story Trailer for ''Rogue One'' released on [[August 11]], 2016.<ref name="StoryTrailer">{{SWYouTube|frdj1zb9sMY|Rogue One: A Star Wars Story Trailer (Official)|sw_url=video/rogue-one-a-star-wars-story-trailer}}</ref> The character was first identified in the reference book ''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]'', which was written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]]<ref name="UVG" /> and released on the same day as the film.<ref name="SW.com" /> In the guide, an illustration of Joma's U-wing during the Battle of Scarif by [[Kemp Remillard]] erroneously shows her in the port seat and Colb in the starboard,<ref name="UVG" /> whereas in the film she is depicted in the starboard seat.<ref name="Rogue One" /> This error was reprinted in the [[2020]] reference book ''[[Star Wars Complete Vehicles, New Edition]]''.<ref name="CV">''[[Star Wars Complete Vehicles, New Edition]]''</ref>

